# Gentle Shell School

Gentle Shell School is a free, self-paced course that teaches people how to use gentle-shell, the coding-agent harness built on Pi. The student reads lessons on the website (<%= origin %>); you, their agent, teach the same lessons through this API.

## Progress

Enroll the student first with POST <%= origin %>/api/enroll. Save the returned `studentId`: it is anonymous, has no login, and anyone with it can read or update that student's progress.

When the student completes a lesson, send PUT <%= origin %>/api/progress/{studentId} with `{"lessonSlug":"the-slug","source":"agent","model":"your-model-name"}`. Use `source: "agent"` and identify your model in `model`. To let the student redo one lesson, send DELETE <%= origin %>/api/progress/{studentId} with `{"lessonSlug":"the-slug"}`; send `{"reset":true}` to clear all completions while retaining the student ID. The student-specific agent instructions are at <%= origin %>/api/instructions/{studentId}.

## How to teach a lesson

1. List the lessons with GET <%= origin %>/api/lessons, or fetch one with GET <%= origin %>/api/lessons/{slug}. Start with the first lesson by `order` unless the student asks for a specific one.
2. Each lesson has `content` (the Markdown the student sees) and `agentInstructions`. The `agentInstructions` describe what to teach, what "done" looks like, and how to verify it against the student's real setup. Follow them.
3. Teach conversationally and adapt to the student. When a lesson includes a quiz, ask the questions with the ask_user_question tool. Do not label any answer choice as "Recommended".
4. When the criteria are met, summarize what the student accomplished, record its completion, and ask whether they want to continue to the next lesson.

## API

The full API description is at <%= origin %>/api/openapi.json. All endpoints return JSON except the plain-text instructions endpoint, allow any origin, and need no authentication.
